{{also|coïncide|coïncidé}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} ''[[coïncider]]'', from {{etyl|ML.}} ''[[coincidere]]'' ([[co-]] + [[incidere]])

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-coincide.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|coincides|coinciding|coincided}}

# To occupy exactly the same [[space]].
#: ''The two squares '''coincide''' nicely.''
# To occur at the same time.
#: ''The conference will '''coincide''' with his vacation.''
# To [[correspond]], [[concur]], or [[agree]].
#: ''Our ideas '''coincide''', except in certain areas.''

